# Line-ending policy (M47). The LAST matching line wins, so the byte-locked
# directories stay at the bottom.

# Default: anything git resolves as text is stored LF in the index and checked
# out LF on every platform. Without this line a path is `unspecified` and its
# handling falls back to the local `core.autocrlf`, which differs per machine
# and per CI image.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary families declared outright rather than left to git's content sniff.
# The sniff (a NUL byte in the first 8000) classifies all of these correctly
# today, but it is a heuristic over file CONTENT and it has already failed in
# this repo: a Windows `actions/checkout` CRLF-converted the .txt/.qsf
# artifacts and tripped the md5 lock during M20's review. Declaring them
# removes the guess. `.svg` is deliberately absent — `pkgdown/favicon/
# favicon.svg` is genuine text and is normalized like any other text file.
*.rda binary
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.docx binary
*.zip binary

# Distribution artifacts are byte-exact (md5-locked to the hitop_artifacts
# manifest, D-016): never apply line-ending conversion on checkout.
inst/extdata/** -text

# The pkgdown site's download copies are byte-locked to the same manifest
# (D-033) — same reason, same rule.
pkgdown/assets/downloads/** -text
